-- title:
--   At most twenty prepared edge sets
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be an abelian group, $H=G[2]$, $K=G[3]$, and $P_\chi(S)=\sum_{x\in S}\chi(x)$ for a complex additive character $\chi$ (so $\chi(x+y)=\chi(x)\chi(y)$). Write $Q_S$ for ordered-sum counts and $\mathcal O_B(S)=(Q_S,(P_{\chi_i}(S))_i)$ for a bank $B=(\chi_i)$. For a finite support bound $U$, partial half solver $h$, and arbitrary Boolean precheck $c$, if $|U|\le6$, then $$|\operatorname{PreparedEdges}(U,h,c)|\le20.$$
--
--   The precheck can only reduce the candidate family.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, Couret — Additive reconstruction: STROBO-4, singleton collisions and RECOH formal proof artifacts, https://zenodo.org/records/23980513; archive COURET_MATHEMATIQUES_20261105.zip, SHA-256 19a3b59aee930df74cab79c27b29e014843bd17179a26fef1261ed6b5a651ab7; file RECOH/lean/RecohPreparedDecoder.lean, lines 64–68; source file SHA-256 f6373eabc2c71ec81235339b571dd8d279e57b6848a6d8ac04fcaaf979efd104; theorem Couret.STROBO2TORS.recoh_prepared_edge_sets_card_le_twenty

